sentences.l:
and not, then, was he destined, having escaped the evil death-fates,
exulting in his horses and chariot, from the ships
back to return to windy Ilios;

and slantwise darting break about themselves the forest,
cutting it at the root, and beneath a din of teeth
arises, until someone, having struck, takes the life out of one;

And they with stones from the well-built towers
threw, defending themselves and their huts
and the swift-faring ships;

and like snowflakes they fell to the ground,
which a hard-blowing wind, having shaken the shadowy clouds,
down poured, thick, upon the much-nourishing earth;
